    "description": "The image depicts what happens when the preparation of onion epidermis fails. The sample, stained with calcofluor, was not rinsed well enough and was bunched up during mounting on a glass slide. Despite failing at proper sample preparation, this was captured to showcase that sometimes mistakes can lead to a colorful and ethereal images.\n\nThe image was taken during the PhD Course (Advanced Methods in Light Microscopy) offered at the Center for Advanced Bioimaging (Frederiksberg Campus).\n\nThis image was a joint winner of the 3rd Danish BioImaging Microscopy Image Contest 2026",
