  {
    "accession": "S-BIAD3974",
    "slug": "nano-ice-skaters",
    "title": "Nano Ice skaters",
    "creator": "Hélène Roberge",
    "affiliation": "VIB-BIC Leuven",
    "caption": "Frozen dust particles resemble tiny skaters in a chance microscopic winter scene.",
    "alt": "Small grey clusters resemble figures skating over a diagonally ridged, snowy-looking surface.",
    "recognition": "Runner-up · Euro-BioImaging Four Seasons of the Invisible — Winter",
    "imageUuid": "7a77d052-2387-4eed-aa5d-a2a1e8fcf267",
    "representationUuid": "a17fa325-2508-4f72-9f5e-934a8142d142",
    "description": "We used cryo 3D FIB/SEM to develop a new approach for characterizing fouling induced by biomolecule filtration through polymeric membranes. During observation, some dust particles were found frozen onto the side of the sample and on the sample holder. Those particles resemble tiny figures in motion, perhaps ice skating or engaged in a playful snowball fight. What might otherwise go unnoticed becomes a lively winter scene, where chance and imagination bring character to the microscopic world.\n\nRunner-up image of Euro-BioImaging's Contest: Four Seasons of the Invisible - Winter.",
